 and hands out its own interface address as the default gateway\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"VyOS eth2 configured 10.50.10.254/24 with a DHCP shared-network LAN-A pool 10.50.10.100-200 and option default-router 10.50.10.254 (cmd-9b68e20f84cd41d3). Post-config show interfaces/dhcp stats confirm eth2 address and 101 available leases in the pool (cmd-072be4af398f429e). node3's acquired lease independently confirms the router hands out 10.50.10.254 as gateway (cmd-de8b845018ca4a6c).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-9b68e20f84cd41d3\",\"cmd-072be4af398f429e\",\"cmd-de8b845018ca4a6c\"]},{\"id\":\"node2-dhcp-lan-b\",\"requirement\":\"node2 (OPNsense) serves DHCP addressing on lan-b and hands out its own interface address as the default gateway\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"OPNsense config.xml updated to add opt1 (vtnet2) at 10.50.20.254/24 and a dnsmasq dhcp_ranges entry for opt1 covering 10.50.20.100-200 (cmd-eb7684dee9434647), applied via configctl interface reconfigure (cmd-187b702879094913) confirming vtnet2 carries 10.50.20.254 (cmd-92fc1e2584a14d6d). A pre-existing global dnsmasq listen-interface restriction (lan only) was discovered and corrected to lan,opt1, confirmed by the regenerated dnsmasq.conf listing interface=vtnet0,vtnet2 (cmd-321bb392976840a6). node4's resulting lease with default route via 10.50.20.254 independently confirms the router serves itself as gateway (cmd-7b6a9bcbdeab4fe2, cmd-dc6f6481f35345c7).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-eb7684dee9434647\",\"cmd-187b702879094913\",\"cmd-92fc1e2584a14d6d\",\"cmd-321bb392976840a6\",\"cmd-7b6a9bcbdeab4fe2\",\"cmd-dc6f6481f35345c7\"]},{\"id\":\"node3-dynamic-from-node1\",\"requirement\":\"node3 obtains its addressing dynamically from node1 (the router in front of it) rather than static configuration\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node3's ens7 (facing node1 on lan-a) has no static network config in /etc/network/interfaces or interfaces.d (cmd-c27bf7d50b8f41f5, cmd-df77f58f572a4715); it is instead managed by a systemd-networkd DHCP profile. After node1's DHCP server was enabled, ens7 acquired 10.50.10.100/24 dynamically (proto dhcp) with a default route via 10.50.10.254, and successfully pinged the gateway (cmd-de8b845018ca4a6c).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c27bf7d50b8f41f5\",\"cmd-df77f58f572a4715\",\"cmd-de8b845018ca4a6c\"]},{\"id\":\"node4-dynamic-from-node2\",\"requirement\":\"node4 obtains its addressing dynamically from node2 (the router in front of it) rather than static configuration\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"After node2's dnsmasq listen-interface fix, node4's ens7 (facing node2 on lan-b) acquired 10.50.20.167/24 dynamically via DHCP with a default route via 10.50.20.254 after a systemd-networkd restart to trigger DHCP retry (cmd-7b6a9bcbdeab4fe2), and successfully pinged the gateway (cmd-dc6f6481f35345c7).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7b6a9bcbdeab4fe2\",\"cmd-dc6f6481f35345c7\"]},{\"id\":\"node1-restart-evidence\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol for node1: pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/config/dependent-node state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id 7668189d... captured (cmd-b1767db1e34843aa), reboot issued and acknowledged (cmd-5399a8905987422f), connection interruption observed during reboot, and a new boot_id 072e70a3... confirmed post-restart (cmd-75bd949f20c84b7a), matching the fixed after-executor snapshot. Post-restart show interfaces/dhcp-server output confirms eth2 address and DHCP pool persisted (cmd-8b6534a52ae64564), and node3 (a dependent client) is shown to still hold/renew its lease and reach the gateway (cmd-e1c6b3b7462643c1).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b1767db1e34843aa\",\"cmd-5399a8905987422f\",\"cmd-75bd949f20c84b7a\",\"cmd-8b6534a52ae64564\",\"cmd-e1c6b3b7462643c1\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]},{\"id\":\"node2-restart-evidence\",\"requirement\":